    "final_answer": "Collected course details:\n\nCandidate 1 (from prior steps)\n- Title: Project Management Specialization\n- Provider: University of Colorado Boulder\n- Level: Beginner\n- Estimated duration: ~11 weeks\n- Rating: Not re-verified this step, but previously noted as a well-rated beginner specialization.\n- Main skills: Sprint Planning, Scrum, Project Scoping, Engineering Management, Team Management, Risk Management, Team Building, Team Leadership, Scope Management, Stakeholder Communications.\n\nCandidate 2 (current page)\n- Title: Foundations of Project Management\n- Provider: Google (Google Career Certificates)\n- Rating: 4.9/5 (101,891 reviews; 88.22% 5-star, 10.29% 4-star; 99% of learners liked this course).\n- Level: Beginner level; no prior experience required.\n- Estimated duration: 1 week at 10 hours/week (flexible schedule).\n- Main skills taught (from “Skills you’ll gain”): Organizational Change, Change Management, Project Planning, Organizational Structure, Project Management Life Cycle, Strategic Thinking, Program Management, AI Enablement, Project Management.\n\nComparison\n- Provider:\n  - Candidate 1: University of Colorado Boulder (university specialization).\n  - Candidate 2: Google (industry provider via Google Career Certificates).\n- Rating and learner satisfaction:\n  - Candidate 1: Well-rated (exact score not rechecked this step but previously captured as strong).\n  - Candidate 2: Very strong rating (4.9/5 based on 101,891 reviews) with 99% of learners liking the course.\n- Duration:\n  - Candidate 1: ~11 weeks.\n  - Candidate 2: 1 week at 10 hours/week.\n- Level:\n  - Candidate 1: Beginner.\n  - Candidate 2: Beginner; explicitly states “No prior experience required.”\n- Main skills focus:\n  - Candidate 1: Emphasis on the broader project-management toolkit and team/leadership skills—Scrum, sprint planning, project scoping, engineering and team management, risk and scope management, stakeholder communications.\n  - Candidate 2: Foundational understanding of project management practice—project planning, project management life cycle, organizational structure and culture, change management, strategic thinking, program management, AI enablement.\n\nRecommendation (shorter well-rated option, without enrolling)\n- Both options are beginner-friendly and well rated, but the Google “Foundations of Project Management” course is dramatically shorter (1 week vs. ~11 weeks) while still carrying an excellent rating (4.9/5 with a very high volume of reviews and 99% learner satisfaction).\n- For a beginner seeking a shorter, well-rated introduction to project management, the recommended choice is:\n  - Foundations of Project Management (Google)\n  - Justification: \n    - Short duration (1 week at ~10 hours) makes it easier to complete quickly.\n    - Extremely strong, well-validated rating with many reviews.\n    - Clearly targeted at true beginners with no prior experience and covers essential foundational concepts and skills (project management life cycle, planning, organizational structure/culture, change management, and core PM skills).\n\nYou can consider the University of Colorado Boulder specialization later if you want a longer, more in-depth multi-course sequence, but as a first, short, well-rated step, the Google Foundations of Project Management course is the better fit.\n",
